Dear [Authorized Tester Name],

This email serves as formal written authorization from the [Organization Name=
] team for [Authorized Tester Name] to conduct security testing and penetrati=
on testing of the asset(s) identified below.

AUTHORIZED TESTER

Name: [Authorized Tester Name]

ASSETS IN SCOPE

The following asset(s) are explicitly authorized for testing:

- [Fully Qualified Domain Name / IP / Application]
- [Additional asset, if applicable]

Scope includes:
- [Application layer / APIs / authentication / specified components]
- [Other explicitly authorized components]

Scope excludes:
- [Hosting infrastructure, cloud accounts, third-party services, or other exc=
lusions]
- [Any other exclusions]

AUTHORIZED TESTING WINDOW

Start: [Start Date and Time]
End: [End Date and Time]
Timezone: [Timezone]

Testing conducted by the authorized tester against the explicitly in-scope as=
sets during this period is authorized under this written permission. Testing =
outside this period requires renewed written authorization.

PERMITTED TESTING

The authorized tester may conduct reasonable security research and penetratio=
n testing, including:

- Manual penetration testing and security research
- Reconnaissance and application enumeration
- Authentication and session-management testing
- Authorization and access-control testing
- IDOR/BOLA and privilege-escalation testing
- API security testing
- Input-validation and injection testing
- Cross-site scripting testing
- CSRF testing
- File-upload and file-handling testing
- Business-logic testing
- Information-disclosure testing
- Security-boundary and trust-model testing
- Safe proof-of-concept exploitation necessary to establish vulnerability imp=
act
- Testing of application workflows and security controls
- Reasonable automated testing at a safe rate

TESTING RESTRICTIONS

The following activities are not authorized:

- Denial-of-service or distributed-denial-of-service testing
- Deliberate service degradation or disruption
- Destructive exploitation
- Deletion or modification of production data
- Installation of persistence mechanisms, backdoors, malware, or implants
- Attacks against unrelated third-party infrastructure
- Credential attacks against unrelated users
- OTP, SMS, email, or notification spam
- Excessive automated request generation
- Activity intended to exhaust system resources or materially affect availabi=
lity
- Unnecessary access, copying, or disclosure of sensitive information

Testing must remain safe and non-destructive. Where sensitive information is =
inadvertently encountered, access must be limited to the minimum necessary to=
 establish the vulnerability and it must not be publicly disclosed.

VULNERABILITY HANDLING

If testing reveals a vulnerability capable of causing significant data exposu=
re, account compromise, service disruption, or other material impact, the aut=
horized tester should stop testing the affected functionality once sufficient=
 evidence has been obtained and report the issue to the designated security c=
ontact.

REPORTING

Security vulnerabilities discovered during the authorized assessment should b=
e reported as soon as reasonably practicable to:

[Security Contact Name / Team]
[Official Security Email Address]

Reports should include, where applicable:

- Vulnerability description
- Affected endpoint or functionality
- Steps to reproduce
- Proof-of-concept evidence
- Security impact
- Relevant request/response information
- Recommended remediation

AUTHORIZATION AND SAFE HARBOR

[Organization Name] confirms that security testing performed by [Authorized T=
ester Name] against the explicitly identified in-scope assets, during the aut=
horized testing window and within the limitations stated in this email, is au=
thorized by [Organization Name].

[Organization Name] will not consider compliant testing conducted within this=
 explicitly authorized scope and timeframe to constitute unauthorized access =
or malicious activity.

This authorization applies only to the assets and activities expressly descri=
bed above and does not authorize testing of unrelated systems or third-party =
infrastructure.

Sincerely,

[Organization Name] Security / Organizing Team
[Official Organization Email Address]

